.TH INTEGRATION-QUEUE-WORK 1 "July 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
integration:queue:work \- Run the persistent CDC integration event queue worker.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php integration:queue:work
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B integration:queue:work
command is a persistent daemon that handles Path 3 CDC (Change Data Capture). When an external application (like phpBB) is installed on the same database but is not routed through SPP, it cannot use the IntegrationGateway middleware.
.PP
Instead, SPP generates SQL Triggers for the external app's database tables. When a change happens natively, the trigger inserts an event into spp_integration_events. This command runs continuously in the background, polling that table, extracting the events, and broadcasting them through the Data Mesh using the Saga Orchestrator.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
.B Filesystem Writes:
None.
.br
.B DB Interactions:
Continuously polls the spp_integration_events table for pending records and updates their status to processed.
.br
.B Outbound HTTP Calls:
None directly (delegates broadcast to the DAG Orchestrator).
